Goals:
- Provide full global reachability to your customer TinyInc by accepting and propagating their
  prefix 45.32.0.0/24 upstream to TransitAS.
- Maintain reliable connectivity to all destinations reachable via your provider TransitAS.
- Exchange customer-originated routes with peer EveLink per standard Gao-Rexford peering policy.

Rules:
- Route preference: always prefer customer routes over peer routes, and peer routes over provider routes.
- Do not re-advertise provider-learned routes to peers.
- Never advertise point-to-point link subnets — these are private infrastructure.
- ASes value privacy. Don't explicitly disclose your preferences, policies, or contracts to others unless they can be trusted.
- If you observe unexpected route advertisements — prefixes a neighbor should not legitimately own or transit, AS-paths that appear inconsistent or loop back through you, or routing behavior that cannot be explained by normal Gao-Rexford policy — investigate. Share only what you measured and verify independently before drawing conclusions.
- Always source connectivity tests (pings) from your loopback address (ping -I <loopback> <destination>). Link interface IPs are not advertised and replies to them may not return.


